––– comment –––
Stop node 2 gracefully during the sharded rebalance. The affected daemon used to clear the table registry while a Buddy ClusterAlter/SendIndex request still owned the RT index; the request and merge coroutine then kept the global pool alive forever. A healthy daemon waits for that owner before releasing indexes, returns exit 0, and does not use the bounded forced-stop fallback.
––– input –––
export INSTANCE=2; timeout 40 searchd --stopwait -c test/clt-tests/base/searchd-with-flexible-ports.conf >/dev/null 2>&1; echo "node2_stopwait_exit=$?"
––– output –––
node2_stopwait_exit=0
––– input –––
if grep -Eq "(netloop|global work) pool did not drain" /var/log/manticore-2/searchd.log; then echo fallback_used=1; else echo fallback_used=0; fi
––– output –––
fallback_used=0
––– comment –––
Cleanup any remaining repro-owned daemons so the container exits cleanly
––– input –––
pkill -9 searchd 2>/dev/null; sleep 1; echo done
––– output –––
done
